    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "The error is related to `dw_chnl` which is allocated but never used and also the mbarriers in it are never invalidated. Adding this fixes the reproducer for me:\n```\n    dw_chnl = SharedMemoryChannel.alloc(\"dw\", [1], gl.float32,gl.SwizzledSharedLayout(1, 1, 1, [0]), num_buffers=1)\n    dw_chnl.release()\n```\n\nThe issue is that the compiler detects that `dw_chnl` isn't used past the initialization, and re-uses the memory for the iq buffer. Then the hardware must flush some write to the mbarrier location, which is now part of the tma load buffer.\n\n@pawelszczerbuk could consan detect these missing `mbarrier.inval` calls?",
