    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "The important part is that if the memory is reused you must invalidate the mbarrier first. You can avoid this by either invalidating the barrier properly, or keeping it alive so it can't be reused.\n\nThe `_keep_alive()` call in attn fwd is a bit different, the issue there is that the shared memory buffer is still in use by the TMA hardware until the `tma.store_wait` is completed so we need to tell the compiler not to re-use it.",
